<title>SENEGAL: Senegal cotton output forecast 58,875 T next year.</title>
<headline>Senegal cotton output forecast 58,875 T next year.</headline>
<dateline>DAKAR 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senegal is expected to produce 58,875 tonnes of seed cotton in 1997/98 by increasing the area planted to 56,000 hectares against 52,290 hectares the previous season, officials from the SODEFITEX state cotton company said on Monday.</p>
<p>Senegal's cotton output for 1996/97 was 40,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>SODEFITEX, which is earmarked for privatisation, is 77.5 percent state-owned. The French Compagnie Francaise pour le Developpement des Fibres Textiles (CFDT) has a 20 percent stake, with the West African bank BIAO (Banque Internationale de L'Afrique de L'Ouest) holding the remaining 2.5 percent.</p>
<p>--Abidjan newsroom + 21 90 90</p>
